        "start": 300.0,
        "end": 900.0
      }
    ],
    "text": "Now how do we compute GCD efficiently? Do not use subtraction repeatedly. We use the Euclidean algorithm: while B is not zero, remainder R = A % B, set A = B, and set B = R. When B becomes zero, A is our GCD. Why modulo? Because modulo reduces the larger number exponentially in logarithmic time O(log(min(A, B))).",
